# P01-L sensor-derived layer. GPS off: the synthesized GPS is simulator-truth-derived,
# and the claimed arm must not leak truth into the estimate (slice line 9).
# The name is the firmware's: GPS_TYPE was renamed GPS1_TYPE in 4.6 (AP_GPS.cpp:364,
# :2061) and a defaults line under a name the vehicle does not have is silently dropped
# (AP_Param.cpp:2421-2431) -- which is what happened in run-2026-09-26T07-40-00Z
# (plan section 0.2 item 1, section 4.7). GPS2_TYPE is set for the same reason: a
# second receiver is the other route by which a global position could reach the filter.
GPS1_TYPE 0
GPS2_TYPE 0
# The EKF's fusion delay for external navigation (AP_VisualOdom::_delay_ms).
# 50 ms until FIXER5, tuned when the pose was stale (F2 0.292 s then). Measured
# from the dataflash VISP records of the clean runs (p01l-fix5b, p01l-fix5): the
# published pose arrives at SITL p50 2.5-5.7 ms (sim) after its own validity
# stamp, so 50 ms back-dated every measurement ~45 ms too far in a loop that
# carries ext-nav yaw. 10 ms is the pin's default (AP_VisualOdom.cpp:83) and sits
# inside the measured band (p50 3-6 ms, burst tail p90 42-200 ms).
# Range 0-250 ms (AP_VisualOdom.cpp:77-83).
VISO_DELAY_MS 10
# Fusion noise floors, left at firmware defaults and recorded
# (AP_VisualOdom.cpp:85-105: VEL 0.1 m/s, POS 0.2 m, YAW 0.2 rad).
# Quality cannot carry -1 on VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE at af85259
# (GCS_Common.cpp:4150 hardcodes quality 0), so the health gate lives in the
# adapter (section 6 H-bounds), and VISO_QUAL_MIN stays 0 (AP_VisualOdom.cpp:109-115).
VISO_QUAL_MIN 0
# EKF failsafe action on estimator loss: Land (the firmware default made explicit;
# ArduCopter/config.h:112-113, ArduCopter/parameters.cpp:268-273).
FS_EKF_ACTION 1
